  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A flat surface of a thin uniform disk <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is glued to a horizontal table. Another thin uniform disk&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;and with the same radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;rolls without slipping on the circumference of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>, as shown in the figure. A flat surface of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> also lies on the plane of the table. The center of mass of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> has fixed angular speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&omega;</mi></math>&nbsp;about the vertical axis passing through the center of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. The angular momentum of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mi>M</mi><mi>&omega;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;with respect to the center of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. Which of the following is the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>?</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/35a7eb5c-0819-40c8-b88c-662a016b0a3f-image.png\" style=\"width: 153px; height: 200px;\" />​​​​​​​</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "W2DCc",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
